{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam Ali (a.s.)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَّا تَبِيْدُ مَعَالِمُهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAL LAA TABEEDU MA'AALIMUH\nGlory be to Him Whose hallmarks never perish!\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَّا تَنْقُصُ خَزَآئِنُهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAL LAA TANQUSU KHAZAAA'INUH\nGlory be to Him Whose treasures never diminish!\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَا يَضْمَحِلُّ فَخْرُهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAL LAA YADMAHILLU FAKHRUH\nGlory be to Him Whose glory never vanishes!\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَّا يَنْفَدُ مَا عِنْدَهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAL LAA YANFADU MAA I'NDAH\nGlory be to Him Whose possessions never run out!\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَّا يَنْقَطِعُ مُدَّتُهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAL LAA YANQATI'U MUDDATUH\nGlory be to Him Whose term never ends!",
  "merits": "Shaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid Ibn Tawus record that Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said: 'One who offers the four-unit prayer of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) will be as free of sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.' It consists of four units (in sets of two): in each unit, recite Surah al-Fatihah once and Surah al-Tawhid fifty times."
}
